WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.160
Read this slide as four
owned integration contracts.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:08.400
The context adapter packages versioned
stories, API contracts and test

00:00:08.464 --> 00:00:12.840
revisions. Unresolved behavior blocks
approval of the affected cases.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:16.800
The model adapter accepts that
bundle and its configuration,

00:00:16.848 --> 00:00:21.920
then returns a proposed patch. A timeout
or quota failure produces no candidate.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.587
Retries are bounded and recorded.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:28.560
The runner accepts an approved
test commit and run manifest.

00:00:28.747 --> 00:00:33.360
It executes deterministic checks,
preserves the original exit status,

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:36.520
retains raw evidence, and then
cleans up the environment.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:41.760
The evidence adapter indexes those
artifacts using traceable run identifiers.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:45.920
Missing joins remain unknown.
AI can draft a read-only

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:50.000
explanation; it cannot turn missing
or failed evidence into a pass.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.880
These contracts connect
the controlled execution

00:00:52.927 --> 00:00:55.680
environment to traceable
API test evidence.
